PATENT SPECIFICATION: SYSTEM AND METHOD FOR PREDICTIVE AERO-THERMAL REGENERATIVE BRAKING (PTA-RB)\
\
1. FIELD OF THE INVENTION\
The present invention relates generally to electric vehicle (EV) energy management systems. More specifically, it relates to an optimized control logic for regenerative braking that integrates real-time aerodynamic drag modeling and electrochemical thermal mapping to maximize energy recovery and drivetrain longevity.\
\
2. BACKGROUND OF THE INVENTION\
Current regenerative braking systems primarily utilize reactive feedback loops based on motor RPM and battery State of Charge (SoC). These systems suffer from "Regen Gaps" where energy recovery is abruptly limited due to cold battery temperatures or high SoC, causing inconsistent braking feel and energy loss. Furthermore, conventional systems do not decouple aerodynamic drag from total requested deceleration, leading to sub-optimal motor loading and increased inverter thermal stress at high velocities.\
\
3. SUMMARY OF THE INVENTION\
The present invention, PTA-RB (Predictive Aero-Thermal Regenerative Braking), solves the aforementioned problems by introducing a multi-layer predictive control architecture. The system comprises:\
